mlk","id":14807744,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODA3NzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14807744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk","html_url":"https://github.com/pmlk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmlk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-02-20T21:31:10Z","updated_at":"2021-02-20T21:31:10Z","body":"Just speculating about possible past concerns of adding \".\" to `sys.path`:\r\n\r\nThere may be a conflict between the installed `alembic` package and the `./alembic/` folder (\"python package\") when alembic was initialized with `alembic init alembic` as described in [the docs](https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/tutorial.html#creating-an-environment). It may at least cause some confusion.\r\nI know there is no `./alembic/__init__.py` file so technically `./alembic/` wouldn't be a python package. However, maybe the `__init__.py` file needs to be added in order to fix this issue?\r\nMaybe it would be more advisable to initialize alembic with another folder name, say `alembic init migrations`? Should that be reflected in the docs?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/782752502/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"